// src/kernel/boot/witness/r64v2_tools.pdx — R64v2 (paideia-os#1976/#1977)
//
// Dormant symbol-linkage scaffold for the satellite volume-tool ELF
// pipeline (mkfs.pdxfs, mount.pdxfs, umount.pdxfs — tmpfs-seeded by
// bin_seeds.pdx's bs_mkfs_pdxfs_seed / bs_mount_pdxfs_seed /
// bs_umount_pdxfs_seed blocks).
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What this witness proves
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//   (A) `r64v2_tools_witness` links into build/kernel.elf and is
//       reachable as a `call r64v2_tools_witness` from kernel_main.pdx's
//       boot_continue_after_ring3, immediately after
//       `call r86_relative_path_witness;` and before `call
//       present_boot_ready;` — last in the ring-0 witness chain, same
//       slot precedent r86_relative_path_witness itself established.
//   (B) Nothing else. The body is a symbol-existence scaffold that
//       returns 0 without forking or execve-ing /bin/mkfs.pdxfs.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Why the body is deferred — the SAME structural limitation
// r86_relative_path.pdx and r56_meta.pdx document
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// A real exercise of "fork a child, execve /bin/mkfs.pdxfs --dry-run
// /tmp/t.img, wait, assert exit 0" needs sys_execve_shim (src/kernel/
// core/syscall/handlers/sys_execve_shim.pdx), because that is the ONLY
// execve path that resolves a PATH (as opposed to an already-loaded
// image pointer, sys_execve_body's own contract) through the VFS/tmpfs.
// sys_execve_shim validates and copies its path/argv/envp arguments via
// user_ptr_ok / user_read_str_via_walk / user_read_bytes_via_walk, all of
// which resolve the caller-supplied VA against the CURRENT task's real
// page tables.
//
// This call site — inside boot_continue_after_ring3, before the single
// `call enter_userland_initial;` that hands off to init (see kernel_main.
// pdx's "#1604: THE INIT RING-3 HANDOFF — sole read site") — runs with no
// user task yet scheduled: _current_tcb is unset (or points at init's
// not-yet-executing TCB), so every one of those walkers would resolve a
// .bss scratch VA against either no mapping (-EFAULT) or a kernel-only
// page. Exactly the limitation r86_relative_path.pdx's header documents
// for sys_chdir_body / sys_getcwd_body, and r56_meta.pdx's documents for
// the sibling VFS-metadata syscall bodies. enter_userland_initial is a
// ONE-WAY iretq — kernel_main never regains control afterward — so there
// is no later point in the ring-0 witness chain where a real user aspace
// could exist either.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Where the real exercise runs instead
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// tools/run-smoke.sh's `boot_r64v2_tools` mode drives the ACTUAL
// interactive shell (a real ring-3 task with a real user aspace) through
// `mkfs.pdxfs --dry-run /tmp/t.img` via QEMU's serial console — mirroring
// boot_r17_shell_child_process's `true\nexit\n` precedent and
// boot_r86_relative_path's "drive it through the real shell" approach —
// and diffs the resulting log against
// tests/r64v2/expected-tools-mkfs-dry-run.golden. That mechanism
// sidesteps the walker limitation entirely because the shell IS a real
// ring-3 task; it needs no kernel-side witness file to do it.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Wire posture at R64v2
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// WIRED (unconditionally) into kernel_main.pdx's boot_continue_after_ring3,
// same posture as r86_relative_path_witness: the body is a plain
// immediate-return scaffold with zero side effects (no memory writes, no
// nested calls), so wiring it costs one `call` + `ret` at boot.
//
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Reserved-label discipline
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
// Labels prefixed `r64v2t_` throughout (none needed — the body has no
// branches).

module R64v2Tools = structure {

  // ==========================================================================
  // r64v2_tools_witness() -> u64
  //
  //   Returns 0 (SKIP sentinel — this scaffold has no real/SKIP-code
  //   contract of its own to defend, unlike r86_relative_path_witness's
  //   sysno-86 convention; 0 just means "linked, ran, did nothing"). The
  //   body is a scaffold — it does not touch sys_fork_body /
  //   sys_execve_shim / sys_wait4. See the module header's "Why the body
  //   is deferred" section for the full rationale.
  //
  //   Alignment: entry rsp%16==8 (SysV, called from a leaf `call` site in
  //   kernel_main.pdx's boot_continue_after_ring3). One push (rbp) lands
  //   rsp%16==0 (aligned for any future nested call added if this ever
  //   grows a real synthetic-aspace exercise). Matching pop restores rbp
  //   for the caller.
  // ==========================================================================
  pub let r64v2_tools_witness : () -> u64 !{sysreg, mem} @{boot} =
    fn () -> unsafe {
      effects: { sysreg, mem },
      capabilities: { boot },
      justification: "R64v2 (paideia-os#1976/#1977). Dormant symbol-linkage scaffold for the satellite volume-tool ELF pipeline (mkfs.pdxfs/mount.pdxfs/umount.pdxfs, tmpfs-seeded by bin_seeds.pdx). Symbol-existence witness: links into build/kernel.elf, wired unconditionally into kernel_main.pdx's boot_continue_after_ring3 (last in the ring-0 witness chain, immediately after r86_relative_path_witness and before present_boot_ready), and returns 0 without invoking sys_fork_body/sys_execve_shim/sys_wait4_body. Real invocation is deferred to the REAL ring-3 shell — tools/run-smoke.sh's boot_r64v2_tools mode drives an actual `mkfs.pdxfs --dry-run /tmp/t.img` command through the actual shell binary and diffs the resulting serial log against tests/r64v2/expected-tools-mkfs-dry-run.golden — because sys_execve_shim (the only execve path that resolves a PATH through the VFS, as opposed to sys_execve_body's already-loaded-image contract) resolves its path/argv/envp arguments via user_ptr_ok / user_read_str_via_walk / user_read_bytes_via_walk, which validate the caller-supplied VA against the CURRENT task's real page tables; a kernel-side call site at this point in boot — before enter_userland_initial's one-way ring-3 hand-off — has no such task, exactly the limitation src/kernel/boot/witness/r86_relative_path.pdx's own header documents for sys_chdir_body/sys_getcwd_body and src/kernel/boot/witness/r56_meta.pdx's documents for the sibling R56.M3 VFS-metadata syscall bodies. Wiring this dormant scaffold in (rather than leaving it unwired) is safe because the body has zero side effects — one push, one immediate load, one pop, one ret. Body: 1-push (rbp) callee-save prologue lands rsp%16==0 (entry %16==8 + 8 = %16==0), aligned for any future nested call a synthetic-aspace exercise would add. Immediate `mov rax, 0; pop rbp; ret`. Matches r86_relative_path_witness / r56_meta_witness / r54_bdev_flush_witness dormant-scaffold precedent. Reserved labels: r64v2t_ (none used — the body has no branches).",
      block: {
        push rbp;
        mov rax, 0;
        pop rbp;
        ret
      }
    }
}
